⚡ SEXTANT SYSTEM
Control Entry Gateway
Operational Manual Section
1. Purpose
The Control Entry Gateway is the primary navigation interface for accessing the major Sextant system components.
It provides a structured entry point where operators, evaluators, or users can select the required operational function.
The gateway separates the platform into dedicated layers:
Documentation
Simulation
Scenario Management
Operations Monitoring
System Validation
2. Gateway Navigation Structure
                SEXTANT SYSTEM
              Control Entry Gateway

                     |
     -------------------------------------
     |          |          |       |      |
 Product   Simulator  Scenario Operations Self Test
 Overview    Engine     Router   Console  Control Room
3. Module Explanation
📘 Product Overview
Purpose:
Provides the introduction and system explanation layer.
Used for:
Understanding Sextant purpose
Reviewing architecture
Learning system capabilities
Audience:
Evaluators
Institutions
Technical reviewers
⚡ Simulator v6.2
Purpose:
The simulation execution environment.
Functions:
Run controlled scenarios
Model system stress
Observe possible cascade behaviour
Generate simulation outputs
Operational flow:
Scenario Input
      ↓
Simulation Engine
      ↓
System Response
      ↓
Risk Analysis
🧭 Scenario Router
Purpose:
Directs selected scenarios into the correct simulation pathway.
Functions:
Scenario classification
Routing logic
Module selection
Example:
FX Shock
   ↓
Financial Stress Module

Infrastructure Event
   ↓
Industrial Resilience Module
🛰 Operations Console
Purpose:
The operational monitoring and visualisation layer.
Functions:
Display system state
Review risk conditions
Observe resilience indicators
Support decision analysis
🧪 Self Test Control Room
Purpose:
Validates system readiness before operation.
Checks:
Module availability
Engine status
Loading sequence
Runtime condition
Example:
Engine        READY
Scenario      READY
Console       READY
System        ONLINE
